<title>GERMANY: Bundesbank details M3 developments in January.</title>
<headline>Bundesbank details M3 developments in January.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bundesbank published the following data relating to M3 money supply in January.</p>
<p> AGGREGATE (in bln marks)	    Jan    Dec   Jan 96  End-Jan</p>
<p>									   level</p>
<p>1) BANK LENDING TO DOMESTIC</p>
<p>   NON-BANKS (total)		  +11.1   +51.7  +21.0  4,796.1</p>
<p>   Lending by Bundesbank	    unch    unch   -0.9   8.7</p>
<p>   Lending by banks		   +11.1   +51.7  +21.9  4,787.4</p>
<p>    To firms and individuals	-7.9    +67.6  -0.3   3,619.8</p>
<p>of which</p>
<p>     short term lending	     -21.3   +23.9  -12.7  596.5</p>
<p>    To public authorities	   +19.0   -15.9  +22.2  1,167.6</p>
<p>2) NET EXTERNAL ASSETS</p>
<p>OF CREDIT INSTITUTIONS</p>
<p>   AND THE BUNDESBANK		 -48.5   +26.2  -34.1   290.5</p>
<p>3) MONETARY CAPITAL FORMATION</p>
<p>   FROM DOMESTIC SOURCES, TOTAL   +7.6    +10.7  +10.3  2,760.7</p>
<p>of which</p>
<p>Time deposits</p>
<p>     4 yrs and more		   +4.9    +5.2   +6.8   801.5</p>
<p>Savings deposits over 3 mths</p>
<p>     notice, savings certificates -5.5    +4.5   -6.2   499.4</p>
<p>Bank debt securities</p>
<p>     in circulation		   +6.0    -1.1   +8.0   1,122.7</p>
<p>4) DEPOSITS OF FED. GOVT.</p>
<p>   IN BANKING SYSTEM		  -6.5    +5.6   -2.1   0.2 5)</p>
<p>   OTHER FACTORS			+4.6    -35.1  +0.4   186.5 6)</p>
<p>   MONEY STOCK M3		     -43.1   +96.7  -21.8  2,139.1</p>
<p>    Currency in circulation	 -3.8    +2.4   -6.8   243.0</p>
<p>    Sight deposits		    -65.4   +52.9  -43.5  605.2</p>
<p>    Time deposits up to 4 yrs     +13.0   +9.5   +10.2  412.0</p>
